---
// ProblemSection.astro - Clean Open-Air Editorial Section (No Excess Cards, No Robot Labels)
---

<section class="section section-white problem-section" id="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header-clean">
      <h2>
        The Costly Reality of Traditional Payment Aggregators
      </h2>
      <p>
        Instant-onboard processors like Stripe and Square are convenient on day one. But as your volume scales past $10K–$100K/month, automated risk rules create severe cash flow bottlenecks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Open-Air 2-Column Editorial Grid (No Heavy Card Boxes) -->
    <div class="editorial-grid">
      <!-- Item 1 -->
      <div class="editorial-item">
        <div class="item-icon-wrap rose-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="2.2">
            <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
            <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="item-content">
          <h3 class="item-title">90 to 180-Day Rolling Reserve Holds</h3>
          <p class="item-desc">
            A sudden spike in sales or marketing scale triggers automated fraud flags. Your hard-earned revenue gets locked into a holding account, choking inventory reorders and payroll.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Item 2 -->
      <div class="editorial-item">
        <div class="item-icon-wrap rose-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="2.2">
            <polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"></polyline>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="item-content">
          <h3 class="item-title">Fragmented Software & Fee Leaks</h3>
          <p class="item-desc">
            When your CRM, checkout system, and subscription tools operate in silos, you end up paying layered gateway fees, un-audited chargeback surcharges, and duplicate processing costs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Item 3 -->
      <div class="editorial-item">
        <div class="item-icon-wrap rose-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="2.2">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
            <line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"></line>
            <line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"></line>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="item-content">
          <h3 class="item-title">Unpredictable "High-Risk" Volume Caps</h3>
          <p class="item-desc">
            Supplements, telehealth, coaching, and subscription brands are frequently re-categorized as "high-risk" without notice, leading to abrupt account terminations and generic bot responses.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Item 4 -->
      <div class="editorial-item">
        <div class="item-icon-wrap rose-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="2.2">
            <line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="23"></line>
            <path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="item-content">
          <h3 class="item-title">Zero Access to Flexible Working Capital</h3>
          <p class="item-desc">
            Because aggregators treat merchants as generic risk data rather than real business partners, they fail to provide customized advance funding when seasonal or ad scale demand hits.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Clean Empathy Divider -->
    <div class="empathy-clean-box">
      <p>
        <em>"If you've experienced delayed payouts, unannounced reserves, or mysterious fee markups — you're not alone. The aggregator model was built to protect their enterprise risk, not your business."</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .editorial-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem 3.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .editorial-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .item-icon-wrap {
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .rose-icon {
    background: var(--rose-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--rose-border);
  }

  .item-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .item-title {
    font-size: 1.22rem;
    color: var(--text-heading);
  }

  .item-desc {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .empathy-clean-box {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .empathy-clean-box p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .editorial-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
